      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day, which is 850 mg three times daily at most. A dose at this level raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, such as 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily**, which is a more typical dosing pattern\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
